uating Circumstances that apply to both inpatient and outpatient authorization requirements.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('bf2f631e-280b-497f-8b92-7a6662b634fb'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99490', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"(1) The only path to authorization after the service has been delivered. The Extenuating Circumstances list is stated to apply to OUTPATIENT authorization requirements as well as inpatient, so it reaches professional home-based services. The listed circumstances are: newborn remaining inpatient longer than the member; member unconscious/unable to give carrier information; retro-enrollment or retro-COB making Molina primary; Transition of Care/Continuity of Care; abortion/sterilization/hysterectomy; the service not being an included benefit of the primary insurance; a baby born to a member with other third-party primary coverage; add-on codes or coding changes during the procedure; and other circumstances as determined by Molina. Mapped by service (all outpatient authorization requirements); no codes named. (2) SCOPE THIS CAREFULLY. Of the five categories listed, only ''Out-of Area/Out-of-Network Professional Services'' reaches the services on this list - i.e. these codes are subject to pre-service review when billed by an out-of-area or out-of-network professional. The ''Home Health'' limb is the home health agency benefit (OAC 5160-12-01 Home Health Services), NOT physician home-visit E/M, and does not make 99341-99350 subject to pre-service review. The document names no codes; nothing here places in-network physician home visits, ACP, TCM or CCM under pre-service review. (3) Blanket rule, applies from the first visit with no visit threshold: any of these services rendered by a non-participating (out-of-network) provider requires prior authorization. Only emergency and urgent care are excluded. Mapped by service, not by code - the document names no CPT/HCPCS codes, but the rule is written for ''all services'', so it reaches physician home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, home health certification/supervision, TCM, CCM and unlisted E/M alike. The same paragraph adds that authorization is not a guarantee of payment. (4) Channel rule effective Jan. 1, 2026: PA requests must be submitted digitally through the Availity Essentials portal. This supersedes the 2025 Provider Manual, which still offers a fax option for the PA Request Form - a PA faxed for a home visit on or after Jan. 1, 2026 is at risk. Applies to every one of these services that requires PA. Mapped by service (the PA process generally); the notice''s own code list covers imaging, wound-care Q-codes and drugs, none of which are on this list. (5) When a member is referred to specialty care outside Molina''s network - which is how an out-of-network home-based palliative practice typically receives a patient - PA is required from Molina. Mapped by service from the ''Requirements Regarding the Submission and Processing of Requests for Specialist Referrals'' section; no codes named. Excludes G0179-G0181, which are physician certification/supervision rather than a specialty referral. (6) Third statement of the out-of-network PA rule, from the ''Out-of-Network Providers and Services'' subsection: all care by non-contracted providers must be prior authorized. The stated exceptions are Emergency Services and dialysis for a member temporarily outside the service area - neither of which covers routine home-based palliative visits. Mapped by service; no codes named. (7) General consequence rule: where PA was required and not obtained, the service may not be paid. Emergency services (as defined by federal and state law) are carved out of PA requirements. This does not by itself establish that any of these codes require PA - it governs what happens when a PA that was required was not obtained. Mapped by service (all services), not by code. (8) Places the burden of verifying eligibility and securing PA on the billing provider - Molina will not treat a missing PA as its own error. Blanket rule from the Claims Information section; mapped by service, no codes named. Practically: check the Prior Authorization Code Lookup Tool per code before each home visit rather than relying on the manual''s narrative list. (9) No retroactive authorization. If one of these services requires PA and PA was not obtained before the service, Molina will not authorize it after the fact through the normal PA channel; the only route is the retro-authorization for Extenuating Circumstances process in the appeal/dispute guide. Blanket rule mapped by service; no codes named. (10) Restates the out-of-network rule in absolute terms in the Utilization Management section: out-of-network services ALWAYS require prior authorization. Applies to every service on this list when the billing provider is out of network. Mapped by service (''out-of-network services'' is unqualified); no codes are named in the document.","appliesToService":"Extenuating Circumstances that apply to both inpatient and outpatient authorization requirements","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Prospective/Pre-Service Review - non-emergent inpatient admissions, outpatient surgery and identified procedures, Home H","quote":"Pre-service review is required for all non-emergent inpatient admissions, outpatient surgery and identified procedures, Home Health, some durable medical equipment (DME) and Out-of Area/Out-of-Network Professional Services.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"All services rendered by non participating Providers","quote":"All services rendered by non participating Providers, excluding emergency and urgent care, require PA.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"The process for obtaining PA","quote":"As a reminder, on Jan. 1, 2026, Molina transitioned to a Digital-Only Authorization Model via the Availity Essentials portal.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid PA Code Changes, effective April 1, 2026"},{"label":"Referrals to specialty care outside the network","quote":"Referrals to specialty care outside the network require PA from Molina.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"care provided by non-contracted, non-network Providers","quote":"If there is a need to go to a non-contracted Provider, all care provided by non-contracted, non-network Providers must be prior authorized by Molina.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Services performed without authorization","quote":"Services performed without authorization may not be eligible for payment. Services provided emergently (as defined by Federal and State Law) are excluded from the Prior Authorization requirements.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"those services that require Prior Authorization","quote":"The Provider is responsible for verifying eligibility and obtaining approval for those services that require Prior Authorization.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"services that require PA","quote":"Molina does not retroactively authorize services that require PA.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Out-of-network services","quote":"Important Note: Out-of-network services always require prior authorization, including authorization for observation days.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0002-4000-8000-00000000a002'::uuid, 'Below is the list of Extenuating Circumstances that apply to both inpatient and outpatient authorization requirements.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
