on delivered care. This consent shall be documented and include:","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"referrals that are made in the patient''s medical record","quote":"Providers need to document referrals that are made in the patient''s medical record. Documentation needs include the specialty, services requested and diagnosis for which the referral is being made.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"prepayment reviews - supporting source documents that justify an amount charged","quote":"Where no supporting documents are provided or insufficient information is provided to substantiate a charge, the Claim will be denied until such time that the Provider can provide sufficient accurate support.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Authorization Appeal or the Clinical Claim Dispute","quote":"The Authorization Appeal or the Clinical Claim Dispute must include new/additional clinical information to be considered.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"retro-authorization for Extenuating Circumstances review","quote":"The specific circumstance the provider feels applied to the request should be noted on the dispute form, documentation to support the extenuating circumstance, as well as the applicable clinical information, should be included with the request.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"Claim Auditing - supporting medical records/documentation as requested","quote":"Additionally, Providers are required, by contract and in accordance with the Provider Manual, to submit all supporting medical records/documentation as requested. Failure