ina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"retro-authorization for Extenuating Circumstances review","quote":"The specific circumstance the provider feels applied to the request should be noted on the dispute form, documentation to support the extenuating circumstance, as well as the applicable clinical information, should be included with the request.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"Claim Auditing - supporting medical records/documentation as requested","quote":"Additionally, Providers are required, by contract and in accordance with the Provider Manual, to submit all supporting medical records/documentation as requested. Failure to do so in a timely manner may result in an audit failure and/or denial, resulting in an overpayment.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'Pursuant to OAC 5160-26-05.1, Molina requires that medical records are maintained in a manner that is current, detailed and organized to ensure that care rendered to Members is consistently documented and that necessary information is readily available in the medical record.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('fd492cbd-ebce-437f-878f-43d5bf5fcf32'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99417', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) General medical record standard applying to all care rendered to members, including home visits. The manual''s content list that follows requires, among other things: legible provider signatures and credentials, a problem list, presenting complaints/diagnoses/treatment plans including follow-up and referrals, medication reconciliation within 30 days of inpatient discharge, allergies, clear progress notes stating the intent for all ordered services, all entries dated, notations regarding follow-up care, and a copy of Advance Directives when in place. Records must be retained not less than 10 years from the last date of treatment. Mapped by service (all care documented in the member record); no codes named. (2) Where any of these services is delivered by telehealth, member (or guardian) consent must be documented, and the manual enumerates fifteen elements that consent must cover - including how telehealth compares to in-person care, the member''s right to suspend or refuse treatment, record-keeping, limits to confidentiality, an explicit emergency plan, the practitioner''s credentials and billing arrangements, a technical-failure contingency plan, prescribing policies, and written consent before any recording. Mapped by service (Telehealth and Telemedicine Services, which are described as a method of accessing Covered Services generally); no codes named. (3) A provider may be placed on prepayment review at Molina''s discretion or at a state program''s request, after which every claim is held until source documentation substantiating the charge is supplied. Insufficient documentation means the claim stays denied until adequate support is provided. Applies to any of these services while the practice is under prepayment review. Mapped by service (all claims); no codes named. (4) Any appeal or clinical dispute of a denied authorization for these services must contain NEW or ADDITIONAL clinical information; resubmitting the original record is grounds for refusal to review. The guide adds that only one submission per service is accepted - a second submission is denied even if it contains new information. Mapped by service (all authorization denials); no codes named. (5) When claiming an Extenuating Circumstance to obtain authorization after the fact, three things must be submitted together: the specific circumstance noted on the dispute form, documentation substantiating that circumstance, and the applicable clinical information. Missing any one of them is a denial risk. Mapped by service (all authorization requests using this route); no codes named. (6) Post-payment and pre-payment audit exposure: records must be produced on request, and failure to produce them timely is itself grounds for denial and overpayment recovery. Molina also reserves the right to extrapolate an error rate from a statistically valid random sample across all claims. Applies to every service billed. Mapped by service (all claims); no codes named.","appliesToService":"Member Medical Records","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"consent to the use of telehealth for services instead of in-person delivered care","quote":"The Member or their guardian needs to have the option to consent to the use of telehealth for services instead of in-person delivered care. This consent shall be documented and include:","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"prepayment reviews - supporting source documents that justify an amount charged","quote":"Where no supporting documents are provided or insufficient information is provided to substantiate a charge, the Claim will be denied until such time that the Provider can provide sufficient accurate support.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Authorization Appeal or the Clinical Claim Dispute","quote":"The Authorization Appeal or the Clinical Claim Dispute must include new/additional clinical information to be considered.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"retro-authorization for Extenuating Circumstances review","quote":"The specific circumstance the provider feels applied to the request should be noted on the dispute form, documentation to support the extenuating circumstance, as well as the applicable clinical information, should be included with the request.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"Claim Auditing - supporting medical records/documentation as requested","quote":"Additionally, Providers are required, by contract and in accordance with the Provider Manual, to submit all supporting medical records/documentation as requested. Failure to do so in a timely manner may result in an audit failure and/or denial, resulting in an overpayment.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'Pursuant to OAC 5160-26-05.1, Molina requires that medical records are maintained in a manner that is current, detailed and organized to ensure that care rendered to Members is consistently documented and that necessary information is readily available in the medical record.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
