r can provide sufficient accurate support.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Authorization Appeal or the Clinical Claim Dispute","quote":"The Authorization Appeal or the Clinical Claim Dispute must include new/additional clinical information to be considered.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"retro-authorization for Extenuating Circumstances review","quote":"The specific circumstance the provider feels applied to the request should be noted on the dispute form, documentation to support the extenuating circumstance, as well as the applicable clinical information, should be included with the request.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"Claim Auditing - supporting medical records/documentation as requested","quote":"Additionally, Providers are required, by contract and in accordance with the Provider Manual, to submit all supporting medical records/documentation as requested. Failure to do so in a timely manner may result in an audit failure and/or denial, resulting in an overpayment.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'Pursuant to OAC 5160-26-05.1, Molina requires that medical records are maintained in a manner that is current, detailed and organized to ensure that care rendered to Members is consistently documented and that necessary information is readily available in the medical record.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('1c4edb3b-b848-4106-8035-7afd555d502e'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) General medical record standard applying to all care rendered to members, including home visits. The manual''s content list that follows requires, among other things: legible provider signatures and credentials, a problem list, presenting complaints/diagnoses/treatment plans including follow-up and referrals, medication reconciliation within 30 days of inpatient discharge, allergies, clear progress notes stating the intent for all ordered services, all entries dated, notations regarding follow-up care, and a copy of Advance Directives when in place. Records must be retained not less than 10 years from the last date of treatment. Mapped by service (all care documented in the member record); no codes named. (2) Where any of these services is delivered by telehealth, member (or guardian) consent must be documented, and the manual enumerates fifteen elements that consent must cover - including how telehealth compares to in-person care, the member''s right to suspend or refuse treatment, record-keeping, limits to confidentiality, an explicit emergency plan, the practitioner''s credentials and billing arrangements, a technical-failure contingency plan, prescribing policies, and written consent before any recording. Mapped by service (Telehealth and Telemedicine Services, which are described as a method of accessing Covered Services generally); no codes named. (3) Separate from the unlisted-code documentation rule: a HIPAA 5010 requirement that a corresponding narrative description of the procedure be transmitted on the claim itself (837P loop) whenever a code whose descriptor contains ''Unlisted'' is billed. Without it the transaction is not HIPAA-compliant. 99499 is ''Unlisted evaluation and management service'', so its descriptor contains one of the listed terms. Mapped by descriptor term, not by code - the document names no codes. (4) A provider may be placed on prepayment review at Molina''s discretion or at a state program''s request, after which every claim is held until source documentation substantiating the charge is supplied. Insufficient documentation means the claim stays denied until adequate support is provided. Applies to any of these services while the practice is under prepayment review. Mapped by service (all claims); no codes named. (5) Documentation is mandatory for every unlisted code billed. The manual specifies it should include a complete description of the unlisted code (plus, for other unlisted-code types, an operative report, invoice, or NDC/dose/route as applicable). For 99499 the operative requirement is a complete written description of the E/M service performed. Mapped by service (''unlisted codes''); 99499 is not named in the document. (6) Any appeal or clinical dispute of a denied authorization for these services must contain NEW or ADDITIONAL clinical information; resubmitting the original record is grounds for refusal to review. The guide adds that only one submission per service is accepted - a second submission is denied even if it contains new information. Mapped by service (all authorization denials); no codes named. (7) When claiming an Extenuating Circumstance to obtain authorization after the fact, three things must be submitted together: the specific circumstance noted on the dispute form, documentation substantiating that circumstance, and the applicable clinical information. Missing any one of them is a denial risk. Mapped by service (all authorization requests using this route); no codes named. (8) Post-payment and pre-payment audit exposure: records must be produced on request, and failure to produce them timely is itself grounds for denial and overpayment recovery. Molina also reserves the right to extrapolate an error rate from a statistically valid random sample across all claims. Applies to every service billed. Mapped by service (all claims); no codes named.","appliesToService":"Member Medical Records","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"consent to the use of telehealth for services instead of in-person delivered care","quote":"The Member or their guardian needs to have the option to consent to the use of telehealth for services instead of in-person delivered care. This consent shall be documented and include:","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Billing of Not Otherwise Classified (NOC) - codes whose descriptor includes terms such as \"Not Otherwise Classified (NOC","quote":"If a procedure code containing any of these descriptor terms is billed, a corresponding description of that procedure is required; otherwise, the Claim is not HIPAA-compliant.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"prepayment reviews - supporting source documents that justify an amount charged","quote":"Where no supporting documents are provided or insufficient information is provided to substantiate a charge, the Claim will be denied until such time that the Provider can provide sufficient accurate support.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"unlisted codes submitted for reimbursement","quote":"If an unlisted code is used, documentation is required for all unlisted codes submitted for reimbursement.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Authorization Appeal or the Clinical Claim Dispute","quote":"The Authorization Appeal or the Clinical Claim Dispute must include new/additional clinical information to be considered.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"retro-authorization for Extenuating Circumstances review","quote":"The specific circumstance the provider feels applied to the request should be noted on the dispute form, documentation to support the extenuating circumstance, as well as the applicable clinical information, should be included with the request.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio — Medicaid Authorization Appeal, Clinical and Non-Clinical Claim Dispute Guide (MHO-PROV-0103, Dec 2025)"},{"label":"Claim Auditing - supporting medical records/documentation as requested","quote":"Additionally, Providers are required, by contract and in accordance with the Provider Manual, to submit all supporting medical records/documentation as requested. Failure to do so in a timely manner may result in an audit failure and/or denial, resulting in an overpayment.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'Pursuant to OAC 5160-26-05.1, Molina requires that medical records are maintained in a manner that is current, detailed and organized to ensure that care rendered to Members is consistently documented and that necessary information is readily available in the medical record.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('81dde84e-0353-4ab1-8d6f-c23518942797'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'modifier_required', '{"answer":"(1) High-value rule for home-based palliative practices, where nurse practitioners deliver most visits. EVERY service billed for an APN must carry the modifier denoting the type of APN who rendered it - not just selected services. Reimbursement follows OAC 5160-4-04 (APRN Services). Mapped by service (''any service provided by an APN'' is unqualified, so it reaches home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, TCM, CCM and unlisted E/M); the document names no codes and does not specify which modifier maps to which APN type - consult the ODM Modifiers document referenced by the manual. (2) Where Molina Medicaid is the primary payer, telehealth claims for these services must carry the GT modifier (plus any other appropriate modifiers). The same sentence governs place of service - see the paired pos_allowed rule. Mapped by service (all telehealth claims); no codes named. Community behavioural health providers follow separate ODM BH manual guidance. (3) General requirement that every telehealth claim carry the correct codes and appropriate modifiers for the plan type and service, with CMS and ODM telehealth billing guidelines controlling the specifics (OAC 5160-1-18). Mapped by service (all telehealth claims); no codes named. Use with the GT-modifier rule above.","appliesToService":"any service provided by an APN [Advanced Practice Nurse]","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"telehealth Claims - Guidance for Medicaid as Primary Payer","quote":"Guidance for Medicaid as Primary Payer: The GT modifier, and any other appropriate modifiers, should be included on all telehealth Claims, and the POS should accurately reflect the physical location of the practitioner*.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"All telehealth Claims for Molina Members","quote":"All telehealth Claims for Molina Members must be submitted to Molina with correct codes and appropriate modifiers for the plan type and service.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'When billing for any service provided by an APN, all services must be billed with the appropriate modifier to denote the type of APN that provided the service.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('1e544e10-40f0-4ec6-8787-83e5b8bdab85'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99342', 'modifier_required', '{"answer":"(1) High-value rule for home-based palliative practices, where nurse practitioners deliver most visits. EVERY service billed for an APN must carry the modifier denoting the type of APN who rendered it - not just selected services. Reimbursement follows OAC 5160-4-04 (APRN Services). Mapped by service (''any service provided by an APN'' is unqualified, so it reaches home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, TCM, CCM and unlisted E/M); the document names no codes and does not specify which modifier maps to which APN type - consult the ODM Modifiers document referenced by the manual. (2) Where Molina Medicaid is the primary payer, telehealth claims for these services must carry the GT modifier (plus any other appropriate modifiers). The same sentence governs place of service - see the paired pos_allowed rule. Mapped by service (all telehealth claims); no codes named. Community behavioural health providers follow separate ODM BH manual guidance. (3) General requirement that every telehealth claim carry the correct codes and appropriate modifiers for the plan type and service, with CMS and ODM telehealth billing guidelines controlling the specifics (OAC 5160-1-18). Mapped by service (all telehealth claims); no codes named. Use with the GT-modifier rule above.","appliesToService":"any service provided by an APN [Advanced Practice Nurse]","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"telehealth Claims - Guidance for Medicaid as Primary Payer","quote":"Guidance for Medicaid as Primary Payer: The GT modifier, and any other appropriate modifiers, should be included on all telehealth Claims, and the POS should accurately reflect the physical location of the practitioner*.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"All telehealth Claims for Molina Members","quote":"All telehealth Claims for Molina Members must be submitted to Molina with correct codes and appropriate modifiers for the plan type and service.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'When billing for any service provided by an APN, all services must be billed with the appropriate modifier to denote the type of APN that provided the service.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
