  ('2c2153ab-e302-4a3d-883a-2f390fa440c4'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', 'G0181', 'pos_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) Molina publishes a list of POS codes that are invalid on its claims. Codes named in that list that a home-based palliative practice could realistically use: 02 Telehealth (stated to be denied for Medicaid as primary payer unless ODM telehealth billing guidelines say otherwise), 04 Homeless Shelter, 01 Pharmacy, and 03 School (valid only for Medicaid BH services). POS 12 (Home) is NOT on the invalid list. Mapped by service (POS rules for professional CMS-1500 claims generally); no CPT/HCPCS codes named. (2) POS is line-level, not claim-level: when a home visit, an advance care planning discussion and a prolonged service are billed on the same claim, each line must carry the POS for the service on that line. The preceding sentence states POS should be indicative of where that specific procedure/service was rendered. Mapped by service (professional CMS-1500 claims generally); no codes named.","appliesToService":"Place of Service (POS) Codes - codes that are not valid and should not be used","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Place of Service (POS) Codes placed on health care professional Claims (CMS-1500) to indicate the setting in which a ser","quote":"If billing multiple lines, each line should indicate the POS for the procedure/service on that line.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'The following place of service codes are not valid and should not be used unless following an exception noted in the list below.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('1843ede1-bd11-47dd-8d25-961e570d074d'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"Molina applies NCCI procedure-to-procedure bundling edits. An E/M service performed on the same day, by the same physician, in conjunction with a procedure bundles into that procedure with no separate reimbursement where the sole purpose of the visit was to perform the procedure. This is an explicit rule about E/M generally, so it applies to the home-visit E/M codes and the other E/M-family codes on this list. Providers must report the most comprehensive CPT code and append the most appropriate modifier when one is required to break an edit. Mapped by service (''an evaluation and management (E&M) code''); no specific codes named. Excludes G0179-G0181, which are not E/M visit codes.","appliesToService":"services/procedures performed in conjunction with an evaluation and management (E&M) code","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'Based on NCCI Coding Manual and CPT guidelines, some services/procedures performed in conjunction with an evaluation and management (E&M) code will bundle into the procedure when performed by the same physician, and separate reimbursement will not be allowed if the sole purpose for a visit is to perform the procedures.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
