  ('eed3e897-1928-4262-8b33-f8874a816b2d'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'units_per_period_max', '{"answer":"(1) The only quantity cap the manual imposes on these services: a PER-DAY, per-provider, per-patient unit maximum drawn from the CMS MUE table, applied through Molina''s claims adjudication edits. Relevant to add-on units of 99417/G0318 and to repeat same-day units of 99497/99498. The manual does NOT publish the MUE values and does NOT state any per-month, per-year or per-benefit-period cap for any of these services. Mapped by service (all HCPCS/CPT codes subject to NCCI); no codes named. (2) Hierarchy rule for quantity limits: where an Ohio Medicaid state benefit limit is tighter than the federal MUE, the state limit governs. The manual adds that a professional organization''s more restrictive standard may be applied above both. Practical effect: the federal MUE is a ceiling, not a guarantee - an Ohio-specific limit on these services can cut below it, and this manual does not publish those state limits. Mapped by service (all codes subject to MUE); no codes named.","appliesToService":"Medically Unlikely Edits (MUEs) - the maximum number of units of service under most circumstances reportable by the same Provider for the same patient on the same date of service","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"a state benefit limit [that] is more stringent/restrictive than a federal MUE","quote":"In the event a state benefit limit is more stringent/restrictive than a federal MUE, Molina will apply the state benefit limit.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'NCCI editing also includes Medically Unlikely Edits (MUEs), which prevent payment for an inappropriate number/quantity of the same service on a single day. An MUE for an HCPCS/CPT code is the maximum number of units of service under most circumstances reportable by the same Provider for the same patient on the same date of service.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('ca036346-5225-40e2-8a2c-31c1b462ca0f'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) Enrollment gate on who may bill anything to Molina Ohio Medicaid: BOTH the group practice and each individual rendering practitioner must be enrolled (or have applied for enrollment) with Ohio Medicaid, and each billing NPI must have an active Medicaid ID number. This is the single most common structural cause of denial for a newly hired home-visit clinician. Ordering, Referring and Prescribing providers must also hold an active Medicaid ID. Mapped by service (a condition on all claims); no codes named. (2) The enforcement half of the enrollment rule: for dates of service on or after Feb. 1, 2023 Molina denies claims from unenrolled or inactive providers, returning remit code N767. The remedy is enrolling or reactivating with ODM through the PNM system - the denial is not appealable on clinical grounds. Applies to every service on this list. Mapped by service (all claims); no codes named. (3) Telehealth delivery of these services is limited to participating (in-network) providers. A non-participating home-based palliative practice cannot rely on telehealth as an access route without addressing the separate out-of-network PA requirement. Mapped by service (Telehealth and Telemedicine Services, described as a method of accessing Covered Services generally); no codes named.","appliesToService":"Medicaid ID Requirements - Providers at both the group practice and individual levels","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Claims for unenrolled or inactive Providers","quote":"For dates of service on or after Feb. 1, 2023, Molina denies Claims for unenrolled or inactive Providers.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Telehealth and Telemedicine Services - Services must be obtained from a participating Provider","quote":"Services must be obtained from a participating Provider.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'In order to comply with federal rule 42 CFR 438.602, the ODM requires Providers at both the group practice and individual levels to be enrolled or apply for enrollment with Ohio Medicaid and to have an active Medicaid Identification (ID) Number for each billing National Provider Identifier (NPI).', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('14863ffe-fd65-4a82-8e45-c744e5d74bd2'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99342', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) Enrollment gate on who may bill anything to Molina Ohio Medicaid: BOTH the group practice and each individual rendering practitioner must be enrolled (or have applied for enrollment) with Ohio Medicaid, and each billing NPI must have an active Medicaid ID number. This is the single most common structural cause of denial for a newly hired home-visit clinician. Ordering, Referring and Prescribing providers must also hold an active Medicaid ID. Mapped by service (a condition on all claims); no codes named. (2) The enforcement half of the enrollment rule: for dates of service on or after Feb. 1, 2023 Molina denies claims from unenrolled or inactive providers, returning remit code N767. The remedy is enrolling or reactivating with ODM through the PNM system - the denial is not appealable on clinical grounds. Applies to every service on this list. Mapped by service (all claims); no codes named. (3) Telehealth delivery of these services is limited to participating (in-network) providers. A non-participating home-based palliative practice cannot rely on telehealth as an access route without addressing the separate out-of-network PA requirement. Mapped by service (Telehealth and Telemedicine Services, described as a method of accessing Covered Services generally); no codes named.","appliesToService":"Medicaid ID Requirements - Providers at both the group practice and individual levels","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Claims for unenrolled or inactive Providers","quote":"For dates of service on or after Feb. 1, 2023, Molina denies Claims for unenrolled or inactive Providers.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2