  ('9bce7b46-2cf0-4727-8608-1f6d61e6fe6d'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) Enrollment gate on who may bill anything to Molina Ohio Medicaid: BOTH the group practice and each individual rendering practitioner must be enrolled (or have applied for enrollment) with Ohio Medicaid, and each billing NPI must have an active Medicaid ID number. This is the single most common structural cause of denial for a newly hired home-visit clinician. Ordering, Referring and Prescribing providers must also hold an active Medicaid ID. Mapped by service (a condition on all claims); no codes named. (2) The enforcement half of the enrollment rule: for dates of service on or after Feb. 1, 2023 Molina denies claims from unenrolled or inactive providers, returning remit code N767. The remedy is enrolling or reactivating with ODM through the PNM system - the denial is not appealable on clinical grounds. Applies to every service on this list. Mapped by service (all claims); no codes named. (3) Telehealth delivery of these services is limited to participating (in-network) providers. A non-participating home-based palliative practice cannot rely on telehealth as an access route without addressing the separate out-of-network PA requirement. Mapped by service (Telehealth and Telemedicine Services, described as a method of accessing Covered Services generally); no codes named.","appliesToService":"Medicaid ID Requirements - Providers at both the group practice and individual levels","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Claims for unenrolled or inactive Providers","quote":"For dates of service on or after Feb. 1, 2023, Molina denies Claims for unenrolled or inactive Providers.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Telehealth and Telemedicine Services - Services must be obtained from a participating Provider","quote":"Services must be obtained from a participating Provider.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'In order to comply with federal rule 42 CFR 438.602, the ODM requires Providers at both the group practice and individual levels to be enrolled or apply for enrollment with Ohio Medicaid and to have an active Medicaid Identification (ID) Number for each billing National Provider Identifier (NPI).', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('f0c398c0-01d9-4346-810f-0116e306158e'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'telehealth_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) THE controlling telehealth rule and the one to check before billing any of these codes by telehealth: payment is available ONLY for medically necessary services listed in Appendix A of OAC 5160-1-18, delivered from the practitioner site. Molina does not reproduce Appendix A in this manual, so whether any specific code on this list is telehealth-billable must be confirmed against OAC 5160-1-18 Appendix A and ODM''s Telehealth Billing Guidelines. No technical equipment or telemedicine provision costs are covered. Mapped by service; no codes named. (2) Telehealth is a delivery channel, not a distinct benefit. A service that is not otherwise a Covered Service does not become payable by being delivered virtually, and no separate telehealth benefit or allowance exists. The manual adds that telehealth services do not include texting, facsimile or email only, and that they include preventive and other routine or consultative visits. Mapped by service (Telehealth and Telemedicine Services generally); no codes named. (3) Telehealth is permitted as a delivery method for Covered Services obtained from participating providers - the manual states Molina supports and encourages it, and eligible provider types are defined in OAC 5160-1-18. It does not enumerate which codes qualify, so this establishes permission in principle, not a code-level yes for any of these services. Mapped by service (Covered Services generally); no codes named. (4) Critical for home-based practices: telehealth may not be billed when the clinician and the member are physically together. A clinician standing in the patient''s home is delivering an in-person service and must bill it as such - a telehealth modifier or telehealth POS on that encounter is a denial. Mapped by service (Telehealth and Telemedicine Services generally); no codes named. (5) Asynchronous store-and-forward delivery of any of these services must be accompanied by an in-person office visit to determine diagnosis or treatment - store-and-forward alone will not support the encounter. Mapped by service (Covered Services delivered by store-and-forward); no codes named.","appliesToService":"health care services identified in Appendix A of OAC 5160-1-18 Telehealth when delivered through the use of telehealth from the practitioner site","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Telehealth and Telemedicine Services","quote":"Services are a method of accessing Covered Services and not a separate benefit.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Covered Services from participating Providers through the use of Telehealth and Telemedicine services","quote":"Molina Members may obtain Covered Services from participating Providers through the use of Telehealth and Telemedicine services.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Telehealth and Telemedicine Services","quote":"Services are not permitted when the Member and participating Provider are in the same physical location.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"},{"label":"Covered Services provided through store-and-forward technology","quote":"Covered Services provided through store-and-forward technology must include an in-person office visit to determine diagnosis or treatment.","document":"Molina Healthcare of Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual + Addendum (July 1, 2025)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0001-4000-8000-00000000a001'::uuid, 'Payment may be made only for Medically Necessary health care services identified in Appendix A of OAC 5160-1-18 Telehealth when delivered through the use of telehealth from the practitioner site.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
