ly authorize services that require prior authorization.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('a1d46ba8-02d2-4ac3-8d67-6be2d67b815e'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"(1) \"Miscellaneous & Unlisted Codes\" is one of the categories on Molina SC''s prior-authorization list effective 02/01/2026, so unlisted E/M (99499) is authorization-territory. Molina requires standard codes when requesting authorization; an unlisted or miscellaneous code should only be requested with supporting material (see the documentation_required rule for 99499). (2) No retroactive authorization: Molina will not authorize a service after the fact when that service required prior authorization. Authorization must be in hand before the visit is rendered. Post-service review is only considered where the provider did not know and could not reasonably have known the patient was a Molina member, or where Molina erred. (3) Blanket payment consequence: if a service on Molina''s PA list is performed without authorization it may not be paid. Emergency services are excluded from the PA requirement, and obtaining authorization does not itself guarantee payment. Scope: applies to any in-scope code whenever a PA requirement attaches (e.g. non-par provider, unlisted code). (4) Same blanket out-of-network rule stated in the handbook: ALL care by a non-contracted, non-network provider must be prior authorized (emergency services excepted). Applies to every in-scope code when the rendering/billing provider is not contracted with Molina SC.","appliesToService":"Miscellaneous & Unlisted Codes","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina Medicaid — Pre-Service Review Guide, effective 02/01/2026","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Services that require prior authorization","quote":"Molina does not retroactively authorize services that require prior authorization.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"Services that require prior authorization","quote":"Services performed without authorization may not be eligible for payment.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"Out of network providers and services","quote":"If there is a need to go to a non-contracted Provider, all care provided by non-contracted, non-network Providers must be prior authorized by Molina.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0005-4000-8000-00000000a005'::uuid, 'Miscellaneous & Unlisted Codes: Molina requires', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('a8880888-7a53-4390-8f7f-699f6191647a'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) Every prior authorization request must carry clinical information sufficient to document medical necessity, including pertinent medical history (treatment, diagnostic tests, examination data) and, for expedited requests, the rationale for expedited processing. The same list also requires member demographics, referring and referred-to provider demographics with NPI, ICD-10 diagnoses, the requested service with all appropriate CPT/HCPCS codes, and the location where the service will be performed. (2) For any authorization request, Molina SC generally expects current (up to 6 months) patient history relevant to the requested service, a relevant physical examination addressing the problem, relevant lab/radiology results, relevant specialty consultation notes, and any other data specific to the request. Effective 02/01/2026. (3) Every note must carry the provider''s signature and credentials. The medical-record standards elsewhere in the handbook repeat this: all staff and provider notes are signed physically or electronically with either name or initials, and all entries are dated. (4) If an unlisted or miscellaneous code (99499) is requested, medical necessity documentation and a written rationale must be submitted with the prior authorization request. Molina expects a standard code to be used wherever one exists. (5) Provider documentation for any encounter must contain a treatment plan and progress notes (alongside the member''s name and date of service, NCCI-compliant coding, and ICD-10 coded to the highest specificity).","appliesToService":"Providers are encouraged to use the Molina prior authorization form provided on the Molina website. If using a different form, the prior authorization request must include the following information","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Information generally required to support authorization decision making","quote":"Current (up to 6 months), adequate patient history related to the requested services.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina Medicaid — Pre-Service Review Guide, effective 02/01/2026"},{"label":"For a complete and accurate medical record, all Provider documentation must","quote":"Have the Provider''s signature and credentials.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"Miscellaneous & Unlisted Codes: Molina requires standard codes when requesting authorization.","quote":"standard codes when requesting authorization. Should an unlisted or miscellaneous code be requested, medical necessity documentation and rationale should be submitted with the prior authorization request.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina Medicaid — Pre-Service Review Guide, effective 02/01/2026"},{"label":"For a complete and accurate medical record, all Provider documentation must","quote":"Contain a treatment plan and progress notes.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0004-4000-8000-00000000a004'::uuid, 'Clinical information sufficient to document the medical necessity of the requested service', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('8dfd3227-809d-4947-8f7c-a48b313cbafd'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) Every prior authorization request must carry clinical information sufficient to document medical necessity, including pertinent medical history (treatment, diagnostic tests, examination data) and, for expedited requests, the rationale for expedited processing. The same list also requires member demographics, referring and referred-to provider demographics with NPI, ICD-10 diagnoses, the requested service with all appropriate CPT/HCPCS codes, and the location where the service will be performed. (2) For any authorization request, Molina SC generally expects current (up to 6 months) patient history relevant to the requested service, a relevant physical examination addressing the problem, relevant lab/radiology results, relevant specialty consultation notes, and any other data specific to the request. Effective 02/01/2026. (3) Diagnosis codes submitted on a visit may only be those confirmed during an actual provider visit with the member; the visit may be face-to-face or telehealth depending on state or CMS requirements. A home visit qualifies as the face-to-face encounter that supports the coded diagnoses. (4) Every note must carry the provider''s signature and credentials. The medical-record standards elsewhere in the handbook repeat this: all staff and provider notes are signed physically or electronically with either name or initials, and all entries are dated. (5) Provider documentation for any encounter must contain a treatment plan and progress notes (alongside the member''s name and date of service, NCCI-compliant coding, and ICD-10 coded to the highest specificity).","appliesToService":"Providers are encouraged to use the Molina prior authorization form provided on the Molina website. If using a different form, the prior authorization request must include the following information","mappedFrom":