"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Information generally required to support authorization decision making","quote":"Current (up to 6 months), adequate patient history related to the requested services.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina Medicaid — Pre-Service Review Guide, effective 02/01/2026"},{"label":"For a complete and accurate medical record, all Provider documentation must","quote":"Only use diagnosis codes confirmed during a Provider visit with a Member. The visit may be face-to-face, or telehealth, depending on state or CMS requirements.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"For a complete and accurate medical record, all Provider documentation must","quote":"Have the Provider''s signature and credentials.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"For a complete and accurate medical record, all Provider documentation must","quote":"Contain a treatment plan and progress notes.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0004-4000-8000-00000000a004'::uuid, 'Clinical information sufficient to document the medical necessity of the requested service', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('ff198bef-062d-4bab-8d8e-89a02e1b6e2a'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99497', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) Every prior authorization request must carry clinical information sufficient to document medical necessity, including pertinent medical history (treatment, diagnostic tests, examination data) and, for expedited requests, the rationale for expedited processing. The same list also requires member demographics, referring and referred-to provider demographics with NPI, ICD-10 diagnoses, the requested service with all appropriate CPT/HCPCS codes, and the location where the service will be performed. (2) Advance care planning discussions must be evidenced in the record: Molina expects documented evidence of the provider-member advance directive discussion and audits for it during routine medical record reviews. MAPPING NOTE: the handbook does not cite 99497/99498; it describes the service (the provider-member advance directive discussion) that those codes report, so this is the documentation standard an ACP claim must be able to support. (3) When an advance directive exists, its presence must be documented in a prominent location in the medical record; the record-content standards additionally require documentation that advance directives, power of attorney and living will were discussed with the member, plus a copy of the advance directive when in place. MAPPING NOTE: stated as a medical-record standard, not as a claim edit; no CPT code is named. (4) For any authorization request, Molina SC generally expects current (up to 6 months) patient history relevant to the requested service, a relevant physical examination addressing the problem, relevant lab/radiology results, relevant specialty consultation notes, and any other data specific to the request. Effective 02/01/2026. (5) Every note must carry the provider''s signature and credentials. The medical-record standards elsewhere in the handbook repeat this: all staff and provider notes are signed physically or electronically with either name or initials, and all entries are dated. (6) Provider documentation for any encounter must contain a treatment plan and progress notes (alongside the member''s name and date of service, NCCI-compliant coding, and ICD-10 coded to the highest specificity).","appliesToService":"Providers are encouraged to use the Molina prior authorization form provided on the Molina website. If using a different form, the prior authorization request must include the following information","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Advance directives (Patient Self-Determination Act) - the discussion between the Provider and the Member","quote":"Molina expects that there will be documented evidence of the discussion between the Provider and the Member during routine medical record reviews.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"Advance directives (Patient Self-Determination Act)","quote":"Providers are instructed to document the presence of an Advance Directive in a prominent location of the medical record.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"Information generally required to support authorization decision making","quote":"Current (up to 6 months), adequate patient history related to the requested services.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina Medicaid — Pre-Service Review Guide, effective 02/01/2026"},{"label":"For a complete and accurate medical record, all Provider documentation must","quote":"Have the Provider''s signature and credentials.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"For a complete and accurate medical record, all Provider documentation must","quote":"Contain a treatment plan and progress notes.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0004-4000-8000-00000000a004'::uuid, 'Clinical information sufficient to document the medical necessity of the requested service', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
