  ('fd6de940-a0ea-408a-804f-8a1af7f7a5c1'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'units_per_period_max', '{"answer":"(1) Per-day unit cap by MUE: the maximum units of a given CPT/HCPCS code reportable by the same provider for the same patient on the same date of service is the CMS MUE value. Molina states no plan-specific visit or unit cap for home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, TCM or CCM - the applicable cap is the federal MUE (or a more restrictive state limit, see the companion rule). (2) Precedence rule for caps: where an SC state benefit limit is more restrictive than the federal MUE, Molina applies the state limit; and a more restrictive professional-organization standard may be used over either. So the effective unit cap on any of these codes is the most restrictive of MUE, SC Medicaid benefit limit, or professional standard.","appliesToService":"Medically Unlikely Edits (MUEs), which prevent payment for an inappropriate number/quantity of the same service on a single day","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"National Correct Coding Initiative (NCCI) edits, including procedure-to-procedure (PTP) bundling edits and Medically Unl","quote":"In the event a state benefit limit is more stringent/restrictive than a federal MUE, Molina will apply the state benefit limit.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0004-4000-8000-00000000a004'::uuid, 'An MUE for a HCPCS/CPT code is the maximum number of units of service under most circumstances reportable by the same Provider for the same patient on the same date of service.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('95a9cda3-424d-4861-821a-3d8d6f594ee4'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'modifier_required', '{"answer":"(1) Molina names no specific modifier for home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, home health certification, TCM, CCM or unlisted E/M. The stated requirement is generic: report the most comprehensive CPT code describing the service, with the most appropriate modifier when one is required (per AMA CPT/HCPCS and NCCI). (2) Modifiers may be appended to a HCPCS/CPT code only when the clinical circumstances justify them; Molina refers providers to the AMA CPT and HCPCS code books for the complete list and appropriate use. No mandatory modifier is named for any in-scope service.","appliesToService":"General coding requirements / NCCI","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Modifiers","quote":"Modifiers may be appended only if the clinical circumstances justify the use of the modifier(s).","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0004-4000-8000-00000000a004'::uuid, 'Providers must correctly report the most comprehensive CPT code that describes the service performed, including the most appropriate modifier when required.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
