  ('d0d2a115-da30-4de7-8a79-829014ef9759'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99427', 'modifier_required', '{"answer":"(1) Molina names no specific modifier for home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, home health certification, TCM, CCM or unlisted E/M. The stated requirement is generic: report the most comprehensive CPT code describing the service, with the most appropriate modifier when one is required (per AMA CPT/HCPCS and NCCI). (2) Modifiers may be appended to a HCPCS/CPT code only when the clinical circumstances justify them; Molina refers providers to the AMA CPT and HCPCS code books for the complete list and appropriate use. No mandatory modifier is named for any in-scope service.","appliesToService":"General coding requirements / NCCI","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Modifiers","quote":"Modifiers may be appended only if the clinical circumstances justify the use of the modifier(s).","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0004-4000-8000-00000000a004'::uuid, 'Providers must correctly report the most comprehensive CPT code that describes the service performed, including the most appropriate modifier when required.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('ceebdfe7-4611-4e90-8675-68b5bacfa927'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'modifier_required', '{"answer":"(1) Molina names no specific modifier for home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, home health certification, TCM, CCM or unlisted E/M. The stated requirement is generic: report the most comprehensive CPT code describing the service, with the most appropriate modifier when one is required (per AMA CPT/HCPCS and NCCI). (2) Modifiers may be appended to a HCPCS/CPT code only when the clinical circumstances justify them; Molina refers providers to the AMA CPT and HCPCS code books for the complete list and appropriate use. No mandatory modifier is named for any in-scope service.","appliesToService":"General coding requirements / NCCI","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Modifiers","quote":"Modifiers may be appended only if the clinical circumstances justify the use of the modifier(s).","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0004-4000-8000-00000000a004'::uuid, 'Providers must correctly report the most comprehensive CPT code that describes the service performed, including the most appropriate modifier when required.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('a582eb3b-142e-45e9-866b-7c63e8983735'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000205'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) Physician services are a covered benefit and the grid names the provider types delivering them: a physician or nurse practitioner, or an RHC/FQHC. Home-visit E/M is physician-service E/M, so a physician or NP may render it. The grid attaches no visit cap to physician services (the one frequency statement in that row is for adult well visits, one per year, which are preventive-medicine codes, not 99341-99350). (2) NPs and PAs are credentialed practitioner types. Where the NP/PA is not licensed to practice independently, the supervising/overseeing practitioner must also be contracted and credentialed with Molina. Critical for home-based palliative practices whose visits are largely NP-delivered. (3) A practitioner may only be credentialed in the specialty for which they have adequate education and training, and must confine their practice to that credentialed area when serving Molina members. Billing outside the credentialed scope is a participation violation.","appliesToService":"Physician Services","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Nurse Practitioners & Physician Assistants","quote":"In certain circumstances, Molina may credential a practitioner who is not licensed to practice independently. In these instances, the practitioner providing the supervision and/or oversight must also be contracted and credentialed with Molina.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"},{"label":"Criteria for participation in the Molina network - Specialty","quote":"Practitioners must confine their practice to their credentialed area of practice when providing services to Molina Members.","document":"Molina Healthcare of South Carolina — 2026 Medicaid Provider Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0004-4000-8000-00000000a004'::uuid, 'This includes services provided by a Physician or nurse practitioner or Rural Health Clinic', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
