  ('5c6732c2-b008-4425-8587-689813fc88e2'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99350', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"(1) Blanket rule. Medical Mutual requires all contracting facilities and professional providers to obtain prior authorization for ''designated services''; non-compliance results in claim rejection. The manual does not publish the designated-service list itself - it directs providers to MedMutual.com/Provider, Policies and Standards, Prior Approval and Investigational Services for the current list. Nothing in this manual names 99341-99350, 99497/99498, 99417/G0318, G0179-G0181, 99495/99496 or the CCM/PCM codes as requiring prior authorization, so this blanket obligation is the only prior-auth statement that reaches home-based palliative E/M; the practice must check the online list per code. (2) Blanket non-payment rule. If a service that requires prior authorization is rendered without an approved authorization, the claim will not be paid. Medical Mutual may, at its sole discretion, perform a retrospective medical-necessity review only where the provider demonstrates one of five enumerated exceptions to plan rules (inability to obtain eligibility at registration, retroactive enrollment/reinstatement, provider or facility system outage with evidence, natural disaster/catastrophic event, or other extenuating circumstances Medical Mutual accepts). Authorization for services already rendered is not a prior authorization and cannot be requested as an urgent/expedited review. (3) For MedMutual Advantage (Medicare Advantage HMO and PPO) members, prior authorization and concurrent review are required as part of the program, on the same basis as Medical Mutual''s other managed care plans. The MA-specific list of services requiring prior authorization is published at MedMutual.com/Provider, Policies and Standards, Prior Approval and Investigational Services; the manual does not enumerate it. Note that the ABN may not be 