used for Medicare Advantage members - to shift liability the provider must instead request a prior written advance determination of coverage (a prior authorization request) before rendering the service. (4) Timing rule, not a visit count. Requests must be submitted in advance of rendering the service. Company response times: non-urgent requested prior to service - within 15 calendar days of receipt; urgent prior to service - within 72 hours; urgent concurrent - within 72 hours (each unless a shorter timeframe is required by law). The manual states no ''after N visits'' authorization threshold for home visits or any other service in the palliative scope.","appliesToService":"designated services (all services on the Company''s prior approval list, billed by contracting facilities and professional providers)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"services in which no prior authorization was approved prior to services being rendered","quote":"Otherwise, claims received for services in which no prior authorization was approved prior to services being rendered will not be paid.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"the MedMutual Advantage Plan (Medicare Advantage) program","quote":"As with other Medical Mutual managed care plans, prior authorization and concurrent review are required as part of the program.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"prior authorization requests for services that require prior authorization","quote":"Prior authorization requests for services that require prior authorization must be submitted in advance of rendering the service and need to allow for the below response times for the review determination.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'The Company requires all contracting facilities and professional providers to obtain prior authorization for designated services. Failure to comply with the requirements will result in rejection of the claim.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
