  ('014bbc82-10a8-4bbb-8e5a-cf87f217a55b'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99490', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"(1) Blanket rule. Medical Mutual requires all contracting facilities and professional providers to obtain prior authorization for ''designated services''; non-compliance results in claim rejection. The manual does not publish the designated-service list itself - it directs providers to MedMutual.com/Provider, Policies and Standards, Prior Approval and Investigational Services for the current list. Nothing in this manual names 99341-99350, 99497/99498, 99417/G0318, G0179-G0181, 99495/99496 or the CCM/PCM codes as requiring prior authorization, so this blanket obligation is the only prior-auth statement that reaches home-based palliative E/M; the practice must check the online list per code. (2) Blanket non-payment rule. If a service that requires prior authorization is rendered without an approved authorization, the claim will not be paid. Medical Mutual may, at its sole discretion, perform a retrospective medical-necessity review only where the provider demonstrates one of five enumerated exceptions to plan rules (inability to obtain eligibility at registration, retroactive enrollment/reinstatement, provider or facility system outage with evidence, natural disaster/catastrophic event, or other extenuating circumstances Medical Mutual accepts). Authorization for services already rendered is not a prior authorization and cannot be requested as an urgent/expedited review. (3) For MedMutual Advantage (Medicare Advantage HMO and PPO) members, prior authorization and concurrent review are required as part of the program, on the same basis as Medical Mutual''s other managed care plans. The MA-specific list of services requiring prior authorization is published at MedMutual.com/Provider, Policies and Standards, Prior Approval and Investigational Services; the manual does not enumerate it. Note that the ABN may not be used for Medicare Advantage members - to shift liability the provider must instead request a prior written advance determination of coverage (a prior authorization request) before rendering the service. (4) Out-of-network rule. For PPO plans, non-network services do not require a referral but are paid at a lower benefit level; to obtain the highest level of benefit reimbursement the services must have prior authorization, obtained before services are rendered by calling the provider number on the member ID card. For HMO plans, elective and non-emergency services from non-network providers are not covered at all unless Medical Mutual determines the particular service is unavailable from a network provider. Directly relevant to a non-contracted home-based palliative practice billing home-visit E/M and the services delivered at that visit. (5) Timing rule, not a visit count. Requests must be submitted in advance of rendering the service. Company response times: non-urgent requested prior to service - within 15 calendar days of receipt; urgent prior to service - within 72 hours; urgent concurrent - within 72 hours (each unless a shorter timeframe is required by law). The manual states no ''after N visits'' authorization threshold for home visits or any other service in the palliative scope.","appliesToService":"designated services (all services on the Company''s prior approval list, billed by contracting facilities and professional providers)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"services in which no prior authorization was approved prior to services being rendered","quote":"Otherwise, claims received for services in which no prior authorization was approved prior to services being rendered will not be paid.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"the MedMutual Advantage Plan (Medicare Advantage) program","quote":"As with other Medical Mutual managed care plans, prior authorization and concurrent review are required as part of the program.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"elective or non-emergency services outside the network","quote":"In order for the Covered Person to receive the highest level of benefit reimbursement, services must have prior authorization. For HMO plans, elective and non-emergency services received from non-network providers are not covered, unless Medical Mutual determines a particular service is not available from a network provider.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"prior authorization requests for services that require prior authorization","quote":"Prior authorization requests for services that require prior authorization must be submitted in advance of rendering the service and need to allow for the below response times for the review determination.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'The Company requires all contracting facilities and professional providers to obtain prior authorization for designated services. Failure to comply with the requirements will result in rejection of the claim.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
