used for Medicare Advantage members - to shift liability the provider must instead request a prior written advance determination of coverage (a prior authorization request) before rendering the service. (4) Out-of-network rule. For PPO plans, non-network services do not require a referral but are paid at a lower benefit level; to obtain the highest level of benefit reimbursement the services must have prior authorization, obtained before services are rendered by calling the provider number on the member ID card. For HMO plans, elective and non-emergency services from non-network providers are not covered at all unless Medical Mutual determines the particular service is unavailable from a network provider. Directly relevant to a non-contracted home-based palliative practice billing home-visit E/M and the services delivered at that visit. (5) Timing rule, not a visit count. Requests must be submitted in advance of rendering the service. Company response times: non-urgent requested prior to service - within 15 calendar days of receipt; urgent prior to service - within 72 hours; urgent concurrent - within 72 hours (each unless a shorter timeframe is required by law). The manual states no ''after N visits'' authorization threshold for home visits or any other service in the palliative scope.","appliesToService":"designated services (all services on the Company''s prior approval list, billed by contracting facilities and professional providers)","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"services in which no prior authorization was approved prior to services being rendered","quote":"Otherwise, claims received for services in which no prior authorization was approved prior to services being rendered will not be paid.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"the MedMutual Advantage Plan (Medic