  ('99674983-e06b-4cff-8bb1-296b85b27d31'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99341', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) For MedMutual Advantage members, medical record documentation must be clear, concise, complete and legible and signed with the provider''s credentials; records must include a treatment plan for the conditions present and use only standard abbreviations, and documentation of all conditions treated or monitored at the face-to-face visit must support each reported diagnosis code, coded to the highest specificity. Requested medical records must be provided within 14 calendar days of written request at no cost. Directly governs the note behind every home visit billed to a MedMutual Advantage member; inadequate documentation triggers financial adjustments on CMS data validation. (2) For any service subject to prior authorization the provider must submit a summary of the service with information supporting medical necessity for each outpatient procedure or service (and for each day of inpatient confinement). Facilities and professional providers must also supply: provider name, member demographics, diagnosis, procedure or service, procedure to be performed, clinical treatment plan, and relevant clinical history. (3) Claim-field requirement. When an authorized service is reported on the claim, the authorization number assigned by Medical Mutual in its response must be reported on the claim (CMS-1500 Item 23; UB-04 Form Locator 63 for the institutional certification number). If the authorization number is missing, payment may be delayed.","appliesToService":"Risk Adjustment - medical record documentation by Medicare Advantage Network providers","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"prior authorization review of a service, procedure, therapy, device or supply","quote":"The provider must submit a summary of the service including information supporting the medical necessity for each day of inpatient confinement, outpatient procedure or service.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Item 23: Prior Authorization Number on the CMS-1500 Claim Form","quote":"The authorization number, as assigned by the Company, in its response must be reported on the claim when the services that were authorized are reported on the claim.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'Medical record documentation shall be clear, concise, complete and legible, and signed with provider''s credentials.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('dcbc9f72-9ff9-4d10-81c6-1a9a59e55ad1'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99342', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) For MedMutual Advantage members, medical record documentation must be clear, concise, complete and legible and signed with the provider''s credentials; records must include a treatment plan for the conditions present and use only standard abbreviations, and documentation of all conditions treated or monitored at the face-to-face visit must support each reported diagnosis code, coded to the highest specificity. Requested medical records must be provided within 14 calendar days of written request at no cost. Directly governs the note behind every home visit billed to a MedMutual Advantage member; inadequate documentation triggers financial adjustments on CMS data validation. (2) For any service subject to prior authorization the provider must submit a summary of the service with information supporting medical necessity for each outpatient procedure or service (and for each day of inpatient confinement). Facilities and professional providers must also supply: provider name, member demographics, diagnosis, procedure or service, procedure to be performed, clinical treatment plan, and relevant clinical history. (3) Claim-field requirement. When an authorized service is reported on the claim, the authorization number assigned by Medical Mutual in its response must be reported on the claim (CMS-1500 Item 23; UB-04 Form Locator 63 for the institutional certification number). If the authorization number is missing, payment may be delayed.","appliesToService":"Risk Adjustment - medical record documentation by Medicare Advantage Network providers","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"prior authorization review of a service, procedure, therapy, device or supply","quote":"The provide