r must submit a summary of the service including information supporting the medical necessity for each day of inpatient confinement, outpatient procedure or service.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Item 23: Prior Authorization Number on the CMS-1500 Claim Form","quote":"The authorization number, as assigned by the Company, in its response must be reported on the claim when the services that were authorized are reported on the claim.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'Medical record documentation shall be clear, concise, complete and legible, and signed with provider''s credentials.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('c124ddd4-e8b9-4039-848a-badd49e545e6'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99497', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) For MedMutual Advantage members, medical record documentation must be clear, concise, complete and legible and signed with the provider''s credentials; records must include a treatment plan for the conditions present and use only standard abbreviations, and documentation of all conditions treated or monitored at the face-to-face visit must support each reported diagnosis code, coded to the highest specificity. Requested medical records must be provided within 14 calendar days of written request at no cost. Directly governs the note behind every home visit billed to a MedMutual Advantage member; inadequate documentation triggers financial adjustments on CMS data validation. (2) Medical record documentation standard, audited by the Clinical Quality Improvement department through random medical record reviews. From age 18 onward the existence of a patient''s advance directive must be prominently documented, and the advance directive itself stored in a consistent and prominent location in the medical record. This is the manual''s only documentation standard touching advance care planning; it is stated as a record-keeping standard, not as a stated billing condition for 99497/99498. (3) Medicare Advantage requirement: network providers should discuss advance directives with patients as appropriate, keep a copy of any advance directive document in the medical record, and each medical record containing one must clearly indicate that the document is included. Medical Mutual actively oversees compliance and may take corrective action where deficiencies are found. Again framed as a record and compliance standard rather than an explicit payment condition on the ACP codes. (4) For any service subject to prior authorization the provider must submit a summary of the service with information supporting medical necessity for each outpatient procedure or service (and for each day of inpatient confinement). Facilities and professional providers must also supply: provider name, member demographics, diagnosis, procedure or service, procedure to be performed, clinical treatment plan, and relevant clinical history. (5) Claim-field requirement. When an authorized service is reported on the claim, the authorization number assigned by Medical Mutual in its response must be reported on the claim (CMS-1500 Item 23; UB-04 Form Locator 63 for the institutional certification number). If the authorization number is missing, payment may be delayed.","appliesToService":"Risk Adjustment - medical record documentation by Medicare Advantage Network providers","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Advance Directives - Medical Record Documentation Standards","quote":"Beginning at age 18, prominently document the existence of a patient''s advance directive.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Advance Directive of Covered Person (Medicare Advantage Network providers)","quote":"Medicare Advantage Network providers should discuss advance directives with their patients as appropriate and keep a copy of any advance directive document in the medical record.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"prior authorization review of a service, procedure, therapy, device or supply","quote":"The provider must submit a summary of the service including information supporting the medical necessity for each day of inpatient confinement, outpatient procedure or service.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Item 23: Prior Authorization Number on the CMS-1500 Claim Form","quote":"The authorization number, as assigned by the Company, in its response must be reported on the claim when the services that were authorized are reported on the claim.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'Medical record documentation shall be clear, concise, complete and legible, and signed with provider''s credentials.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
