y for each outpatient procedure or service (and for each day of inpatient confinement). Facilities and professional providers must also supply: provider name, member demographics, diagnosis, procedure or service, procedure to be performed, clinical treatment plan, and relevant clinical history. (5) Claim-field requirement. When an authorized service is reported on the claim, the authorization number assigned by Medical Mutual in its response must be reported on the claim (CMS-1500 Item 23; UB-04 Form Locator 63 for the institutional certification number). If the authorization number is missing, payment may be delayed.","appliesToService":"Risk Adjustment - medical record documentation by Medicare Advantage Network providers","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Advance Directives - Medical Record Documentation Standards","quote":"Beginning at age 18, prominently document the existence of a patient''s advance directive.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Advance Directive of Covered Person (Medicare Advantage Network providers)","quote":"Medicare Advantage Network providers should discuss advance directives with their patients as appropriate and keep a copy of any advance directive document in the medical record.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"prior authorization review of a service, procedure, therapy, device or supply","quote":"The provider must submit a summary of the service including information supporting the medical necessity for each day of inpatient confinement, outpatient procedure or service.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Item 23: Prior Authorization Number on the CMS-1500 Claim Form","quote":"The authorization number, as assigned by the