r must submit a summary of the service including information supporting the medical necessity for each day of inpatient confinement, outpatient procedure or service.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Item 23: Prior Authorization Number on the CMS-1500 Claim Form","quote":"The authorization number, as assigned by the Company, in its response must be reported on the claim when the services that were authorized are reported on the claim.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'Medical record documentation shall be clear, concise, complete and legible, and signed with provider''s credentials.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('e3c10af4-f4eb-4bc0-8953-60135c97e2d6'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99341', 'pos_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) Medical Mutual does not publish its own place-of-service list; it follows the standard CMS POS code set for professional claims (referencing the CMS Place of Service Code Set at hhs.gov). For home-based palliative care this means the CMS home/residence POS codes (e.g. POS 12 Home, POS 13/14 assisted living or group home) as defined by CMS govern - the manual names no permitted or excluded POS code for home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, home health certification, TCM or CCM/PCM. (2) Denial trigger. An incorrect POS, or use of any code that is not a CMS POS code, may result in denial of the service or an incorrect reimbursement amount. Medical Mutual''s clinical claim edit system also validates CPT/HCPCS codes against place of service, so a home-visit E/M code reported with a non-home POS is exposed to a POS-conflict edit (the manual gives the analogous example of inpatient codes 99221-99239 reported with an outpatient POS being denied). (3) Paper CMS-1500 rule for any service rendered in the patient''s home, which is the normal case for physician home/house-call E/M. Item 32 must carry the word RESIDENCE as the facility name and the patient''s own address as the address. Getting this wrong is a claim-completion defect: the manual warns generally that missing or incorrect information delays processing and may result in underpayments or denials. (4) Electronic 837P equivalent of the Item 32 rule: for services rendered in the patient''s home, the service location name segment must contain ''Residence'' and the address must be the patient''s address. Applies to electronically submitted home-visit E/M claims (Payer ID 29076).","appliesToService":"Item 24B: Place of Service (POS) on professional claims","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Item 24B: Place of Service (POS) on professional claims","quote":"An error in POS or use of a code other than a CMS code may result in denial of the service or an incorrect reimbursement amount.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"services rendered in the patient''s home - Item 32, Name and Address of Facility Where Services Were Rendered","quote":"If services are rendered in the patient''s home, the name must be reported with the word RESIDENCE and use the patient''s address as the address in this item.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"services rendered in the patient''s home - electronic claims filing (837P service location)","quote":"When services are rendered in the patient''s home, use \"Residence\" in the service location name segment and the address of the patient.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'The Company follows the standard POS code guidelines, as standardized by CMS for professional claims.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
