  ('d7bf8be3-ec7a-4597-8ff5-1c1994fcd8ee'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99499', 'pos_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) Medical Mutual does not publish its own place-of-service list; it follows the standard CMS POS code set for professional claims (referencing the CMS Place of Service Code Set at hhs.gov). For home-based palliative care this means the CMS home/residence POS codes (e.g. POS 12 Home, POS 13/14 assisted living or group home) as defined by CMS govern - the manual names no permitted or excluded POS code for home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, home health certification, TCM or CCM/PCM. (2) Denial trigger. An incorrect POS, or use of any code that is not a CMS POS code, may result in denial of the service or an incorrect reimbursement amount. Medical Mutual''s clinical claim edit system also validates CPT/HCPCS codes against place of service, so a home-visit E/M code reported with a non-home POS is exposed to a POS-conflict edit (the manual gives the analogous example of inpatient codes 99221-99239 reported with an outpatient POS being denied).","appliesToService":"Item 24B: Place of Service (POS) on professional claims","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Item 24B: Place of Service (POS) on professional claims","quote":"An error in POS or use of a code other than a CMS code may result in denial of the service or an incorrect reimbursement amount.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'The Company follows the standard POS code guidelines, as standardized by CMS for professional claims.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('f90790bf-fb24-4b6b-87a0-a14720c2582d'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99341', 'bundled_with', '{"answer":"(1) Global surgery bundling. All visits or services performed by any provider from one day before through 90 days after a major procedure, for a diagnosis related to that surgery, are included in the global reimbursement for the major surgical procedure and are not separately payable. Major procedures are listed as major surgery, fracture/dislocation care, podiatry procedures, obstetrical procedures and anesthesia. A palliative home visit that falls in a related 90-day global window is at risk of being bundled, even though the palliative practice did not perform the surgery. (2) Visits or services on the same date as a minor procedure are included in the global reimbursement for that minor surgical procedure. Medical Mutual''s clinical claim edits explicitly include global surgical services, so a same-day home-visit E/M related to a minor procedure will bundle unless a separately identifiable E/M modifier applies.","appliesToService":"visits or services performed during the global surgical period of a major procedure","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"visits or services performed on the same day as a minor procedure","quote":"Visits or services on the same day as a minor procedure are included in the global reimbursement for the minor surgical procedure.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'Visits or services one day prior to and up to 90 days after a major procedure are included in the global reimbursement for the major surgical procedure.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
