  ('e00bf7a2-4b82-40fa-8c92-355e374eeb3a'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304'::uuid, 'OH', 'commercial', '99341', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"(1) Who may bill. Medical Mutual contracts directly with APRNs (NPs, CNSs, CNMs, CRNAs). Every APRN must register with the Company and bill under his or her own provider number; APRN services may no longer be billed under a supervising physician''s number (no incident-to style billing under the supervisor). Critical for palliative practices whose home visits, ACP and care management are furnished by nurse practitioners. Non-physician providers, including APRNs and physician assistants, are reimbursed at 85% of the then-current physician fee. (2) Standard benefit exclusion found in most Company policies: no benefits for services that are not performed within the scope of the provider''s license, and none for services not prescribed by, performed by, or under the direction of a provider. Scope-of-practice limits under Ohio licensure therefore govern which team member may bill home-visit E/M, ACP, prolonged services, home health certification, TCM and CCM/PCM. The manual notes these exclusions are typical but not all-inclusive and vary by policy. (3) Enrollment documentation for PAs who will bill under their own number: application through CAQH, plus a copy of the Physician Assistants Certificate to Practice and a copy of the Physician Assistants Supervision Agreement submitted with the required paperwork. A PA on a home-based palliative team cannot have claims processed until this is on file. (4) APRNs and PAs are eligible to sign the Provider Agreement and to apply to Medical Mutual''s networks (HMO, PPO). Failure to sign and enroll may result in a reduction in benefit on their claims - i.e. services billed by an unenrolled NP or PA on a palliative team are paid at the reduced non-network level.","appliesToService":"services rendered by advanced practice registered nurses (APRNs) - certified nurse practitioners, clinical nurse specialists, certified nurse midwives and certified nurse anesthetists","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"standard benefit exclusion - services, supplies or charges not performed within the scope of the provider''s license","quote":"That are not performed within the scope of the provider''s license","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Physician Assistants contracting directly with the Company","quote":"Physician Assistants must provide a copy of the Physician Assistants Certificate to Practice and a copy of the Physician Assistants Supervision Agreement when submitting their required paperwork to the Company.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"APRNs and PAs signing the Company Provider Agreement and applying to the Company''s networks","quote":"APRNs and PAs are eligible to sign the Company Provider Agreement as well as make application to the Company''s various networks (e.g., HMO, PPO). Failure to do so may result in a reduction in benefit.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'not_covered', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'All APRNs must register with the Company to allow their claims to process, using their own provider number. APRN services rendered can no longer be billed by a supervising provider.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
