ioners, clinical nurse specialists, certified nurse midwives and certified nurse anesthetists","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"standard benefit exclusion - services, supplies or charges not performed within the scope of the provider''s license","quote":"That are not performed within the scope of the provider''s license","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Physician Assistants contracting directly with the Company","quote":"Physician Assistants must provide a copy of the Physician Assistants Certificate to Practice and a copy of the Physician Assistants Supervision Agreement when submitting their required paperwork to the Company.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"APRNs and PAs signing the Company Provider Agreement and applying to the Company''s networks","quote":"APRNs and PAs are eligible to sign the Company Provider Agreement as well as make application to the Company''s various networks (e.g., HMO, PPO). Failure to do so may result in a reduction in benefit.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'not_covered', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'All APRNs must register with the Company to allow their claims to process, using their own provider number. APRN services rendered can no longer be billed by a supervising provider.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
