ioners, clinical nurse specialists, certified nurse midwives and certified nurse anesthetists","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"standard benefit exclusion - services, supplies or charges not performed within the scope of the provider''s license","quote":"That are not performed within the scope of the provider''s license","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"Physician Assistants contracting directly with the Company","quote":"Physician Assistants must provide a copy of the Physician Assistants Certificate to Practice and a copy of the Physician Assistants Supervision Agreement when submitting their required paperwork to the Company.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"},{"label":"APRNs and PAs signing the Company Provider Agreement and applying to the Company''s networks","quote":"APRNs and PAs are eligible to sign the Company Provider Agreement as well as make application to the Company''s various networks (e.g., HMO, PPO). Failure to do so may result in a reduction in benefit.","document":"Medical Mutual of Ohio — Provider Manual (October 2025, Z6640 R10/25)"}]}'::jsonb, 'not_covered', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0006-4000-8000-00000000a006'::uuid, 'All APRNs must register with the Company to allow their claims to process, using their own provider number. APRN services rendered can no longer be billed by a supervising provider.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('a9396e2b-59f3-4565-898a-4960420faac5'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000305'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"(1) Blanket rule: a non-participating (out-of-network) provider must obtain prior authorization for ALL non-emergency services before rendering them. Because it is stated for \"all nonemergency services\" with no service or code carve-out, it reaches every code in scope here — physician home/house-call E/M (99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350), advance care planning (99497-99498), prolonged service (99417, G0318), home health certification/supervision (G0179-G0181), transitional care (99495-99496), chronic/principal care management (99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427) and unlisted E/M (99499). No PA-after-N-visits threshold is stated; the trigger is network status, not visit count. The document does not state a PA requirement for these services when rendered by a participating provider. (2) The Ohio Medicaid prior authorization list itself enumerates \"Any service provided by an out-of-network provider\" under the heading \"Services That Require Prior Authorization.\" This is a blanket, service-agnostic entry, so it applies to every in-scope code (99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350; 99497-99498; 99417, G0318; G0179-G0181; 99495-99496; 99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427; 99499) whenever the billing provider is out of network. Note: the same list''s \"Home Care Services and Therapies\" entries (home health aide visits, skilled nurse visits, private duty nursing, social worker visits, therapies) are home health agency benefits and are NOT mapped to physician home-visit E/M — the document names no CPT/HCPCS code for them. (3) MyCare Ohio / Next Generation MyCare (dual-eligible line ONLY — do not apply to straight Ohio Medicaid members): a nonparticipating (out-of-network) provider must obtain prior authorization for any service rendered to a CareSource MyCare member, except in emergencies. Stated in the claims-submission requirements for MyCare Next Generation claims, with no service carve-out, so it reaches all in-scope codes: 99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350; 99497-99498; 99417, G0318; G0179-G0181; 99495-99496; 99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427; 99499. PA is requested by calling 1-800-488-0134. The manual also warns that PA requirements are validated during claim processing and claims are matched to authorizations on file.","appliesToService":"all nonemergency services provided to a CareSource member by \"any provider who is not a participating provider with CareSource\"","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"CareSource Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual (OH-MED-P-1745200c, ODM approved 9/19/2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Any service provided by an out-of-network provider","quote":"Any service provided by an out-of-network provider","document":"CareSource Ohio Medicaid — Prior Authorization List (OH-MED-M-1691262)"},{"label":"any services rendered to CareSource members by \"Nonparticipating (out-of-network) providers\"","quote":"Nonparticipating (out-of-network) providers must obtain prior authorization for any services rendered to CareSource members, except in emergency situations.","document":"CareSource Ohio — MyCare / Next Generation MyCare Provider Manual (2026, dual-eligible line)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0007-4000-8000-00000000a007'::uuid, 'In addition, any provider who is not a participating provider with CareSource must obtain PA for all nonemergency services provided to a CareSource member.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
