submission requirements for MyCare Next Generation claims, with no service carve-out, so it reaches all in-scope codes: 99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350; 99497-99498; 99417, G0318; G0179-G0181; 99495-99496; 99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427; 99499. PA is requested by calling 1-800-488-0134. The manual also warns that PA requirements are validated during claim processing and claims are matched to authorizations on file.","appliesToService":"all nonemergency services provided to a CareSource member by \"any provider who is not a participating provider with CareSource\"","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"CareSource Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual (OH-MED-P-1745200c, ODM approved 9/19/2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Any service provided by an out-of-network provider","quote":"Any service provided by an out-of-network provider","document":"CareSource Ohio Medicaid — Prior Authorization List (OH-MED-M-1691262)"},{"label":"any services rendered to CareSource members by \"Nonparticipating (out-of-network) providers\"","quote":"Nonparticipating (out-of-network) providers must obtain prior authorization for any services rendered to CareSource members, except in emergency situations.","document":"CareSource Ohio — MyCare / Next Generation MyCare Provider Manual (2026, dual-eligible line)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0007-4000-8000-00000000a007'::uuid, 'In addition, any provider who is not a participating provider with CareSource must obtain PA for all nonemergency services provided to a CareSource member.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('75045ba2-5c70-452b-889f-2590fd25171a'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000305'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"(1) Blanket rule: a non-participating (out-of-network) provider must obtain prior authorization for ALL non-emergency services before rendering them. Because it is stated for \"all nonemergency services\" with no service or code carve-out, it reaches every code in scope here — physician home/house-call E/M (99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350), advance care planning (99497-99498), prolonged service (99417, G0318), home health certification/supervision (G0179-G0181), transitional care (99495-99496), chronic/principal care management (99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427) and unlisted E/M (99499). No PA-after-N-visits threshold is stated; the trigger is network status, not visit count. The document does not state a PA requirement for these services when rendered by a participating provider. (2) The Ohio Medicaid prior authorization list itself enumerates \"Any service provided by an out-of-network provider\" under the heading \"Services That Require Prior Authorization.\" This is a blanket, service-agnostic entry, so it applies to every in-scope code (99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350; 99497-99498; 99417, G0318; G0179-G0181; 99495-99496; 99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427; 99499) whenever the billing provider is out of network. Note: the same list''s \"Home Care Services and Therapies\" entries (home health aide visits, skilled nurse visits, private duty nursing, social worker visits, therapies) are home health agency benefits and are NOT mapped to physician home-visit E/M — the document names no CPT/HCPCS code for them. (3) MyCare Ohio / Next Generation MyCare (dual-eligible line ONLY — do not apply to straight Ohio Medicaid members): a nonparticipating (out-of-network) provider must obtain prior authorization for any service rendered to a CareSource MyCare member, except in emergencies. Stated in the claims-submission requirements for MyCare Next Generation claims, with no service carve-out, so it reaches all in-scope codes: 99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350; 99497-99498; 99417, G0318; G0179-G0181; 99495-99496; 99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427; 99499. PA is requested by calling 1-800-488-0134. The manual also warns that PA requirements are validated during claim processing and claims are matched to authorizations on file. (4) CareSource requires prior authorization for unlisted procedure CPT codes. 99499 is the unlisted/miscellaneous evaluation and management code, so this rule applies to 99499. The manual does not name 99499 explicitly; the mapping is by the document''s own category term \"unlisted procedure CPT codes.\" No visit threshold applies — PA is required for every such claim, and the manual adds that submitting clinical information does not guarantee payment. (5) MyCare Ohio / Next Generation MyCare line (dual-eligible) — same rule as the Medicaid manual: prior authorization is required for unlisted procedure CPT codes, which maps to 99499 (unlisted/miscellaneous E/M). The manual does not name 99499; the mapping is via the document''s own category \"unlisted procedure CPT codes.\" Submission of clinical information does not guarantee payment.","appliesToService":"all nonemergency services provided to a CareSource member by \"any provider who is not a participating provider with CareSource\"","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"CareSource Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual (OH-MED-P-1745200c, ODM approved 9/19/2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Any service provided by an out-of-network provider","quote":"Any service provided by an out-of-network provider","document":"CareSource Ohio Medicaid — Prior Authorization List (OH-MED-M-1691262)"},{"label":"any services rendered to CareSource members by \"Nonparticipating (out-of-network) providers\"","quote":"Nonparticipating (out-of-network) providers must obtain prior authorization for any services rendered to CareSource members, except in emergency situations.","document":"CareSource Ohio — MyCare / Next Generation MyCare Provider Manual (2026, dual-eligible line)"},{"label":"unlisted procedure CPT codes","quote":"CareSource does require PA for unlisted procedure CPT codes.","document":"CareSource Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual (OH-MED-P-1745200c, ODM approved 9/19/2025)"},{"label":"unlisted procedure CPT codes","quote":"CareSource does require PA for unlisted procedure CPT codes.","document":"CareSource Ohio — MyCare / Next Generation MyCare Provider Manual (2026, dual-eligible line)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0007-4000-8000-00000000a007'::uuid, 'In addition, any provider who is not a participating provider with CareSource must obtain PA for all nonemergency services provided to a CareSource member.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('2a6282cf-b7d9-48d3-8d40-53aa03103a20'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000305'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99499', 'documentation_required', '{"answer":"(1) A clinical record must be submitted WITH the claim for unlisted procedure CPT codes; claims submitted without clinical records for unlisted procedure codes are denied. Applies to 99499 (unlisted/miscellaneous E/M). This is a claim-attachment requirement, not merely a chart-documentation requirement — the supporting clinical documentation must accompany the claim submission. (2) MyCare Ohio / Next Generation MyCare line (dual-eligible): clinical records must accompany the claim for unlisted procedure CPT codes, i.e. 99499 (unlisted/miscellaneous E/M). Claims filed without the clinical record are denied; the manual instructs providers to submit supporting clinical documentation with the claim submission to avoid the denial.","appliesToService":"unlisted procedure CPT codes","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"CareSource Ohio Medicaid — Provider Manual (OH-MED-P-1745200c, ODM approved 9/19/2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"unlisted procedure CPT codes","quote":"Claims submitted without clinical records for unlisted procedure CPT codes will be denied.","document":"CareSource Ohio — MyCare / Next Generation MyCare Provider Manual (2026, dual-eligible line)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0007-4000-8000-00000000a007'::uuid, 'Claims submitted without clinical records for unlisted procedure CPT codes will be denied.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('533d2286-ea7b-4ffc-88af-f6f2ddd5267f'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000305'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"MyCare Ohio / Next Generation MyCare line (dual-eligible) — a rule about WHO may bill, therefore applicable to E/M generally and to all in-scope codes (99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350; 99497-99498; 99417, G0318; G0179-G0181; 99495-99496; 99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427; 99499): every provider billing for services to a MyCare Ohio-enrolled member must be enrolled with the Ohio Department of Medicaid through the Provider Network Management (PNM) system. The manual states no restriction by specialty or taxonomy code — the gate is ODM enrollment, not provider type. Contracting with CareSource and ODM enrollment are separate processes and both are required.","appliesToService":"services to MyCare Ohio-enrolled members (\"All providers billing for services\")","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"CareSource Ohio — MyCare / Next Generation MyCare Provider Manual (2026, dual-eligible line)","supportingQuotes":[]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0009-4000-8000-00000000a009'::uuid, 'All providers billing for services to MyCare Ohio-enrolled members must enroll with ODM through the Provider Network Management (PNM) system.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
  ('6b5f9fff-fc34-4240-80c5-bb197927feb6'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000305'::uuid, 'OH', 'medicaid_mco', '99342', 'provider_taxonomy_allowed', '{"answer":"MyCare Ohio / Next Generation MyCare line (dual-eligible) — a rule about WHO may bill, therefore applicable to E/M generally and to all in-scope codes (99341-99342, 99344-99345, 99347-99350; 99497-99498; 99417, G0318; G0179-G0181; 99495-99496; 99490, 99439, 99491, 99424-99427; 99499): every provider billing for services to a MyCare Ohio-enrolled member must be enrolled with the Ohio Department of Medicaid through the Provider Network Management (PNM) system. The manual states no restriction by specialty or taxonomy code — the gate is ODM enrollment, not provider type. Contracting with CareSource and ODM enrollment are separate processes and both are required.","appliesToService":"services to MyCare Ohio-enrolled members (\"All providers billing for services\")","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"CareSource Ohio — MyCare / Next Generation MyCare Provider Manual (2026, dual-eligible line)","supportingQuotes":[]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-0009-4000-8000-00000000a009'::uuid, 'All providers billing for services to MyCare Ohio-enrolled members must enroll with ODM through the Provider Network Management (PNM) system.', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
