  ('89878e0d-871b-446e-8eab-08535092b699'::uuid, 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000202'::uuid, 'SC', 'medicaid_mco', '99341', 'prior_auth_required', '{"answer":"(1) Blanket administrative rule: the plan''s prior authorization requirements also apply when First Choice is the SECONDARY payer. Practices that skip authorization on secondary claims (a common assumption when Medicare or another primary has already paid) will be denied. This is the header note of the 2025 Prior Authorization Information chart and is repeated in the chart''s contacts panel. It is not specific to any service, so it applies to every code in the palliative home-care set to the extent that code otherwise requires authorization. This one IS from the SC Medicaid (First Choice) prior authorization grid. (2) A valid authorization number must appear on the claim form for any service that required prior authorization; a missing or invalid authorization number is listed as a top cause of claim delay, rejection, and denial. Elsewhere the same manual specifies the field: ''Prior authorization number in box 23 on CMS-1500 form (if applicable)'' for professional claims and box 63 on the UB-04. Blanket rule — applies to every code in the palliative home-care set whenever authorization was obtained. SC Medicaid (First Choice) source.","appliesToService":"Services requiring prior authorization","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"First Choice by Select Health of South Carolina — Prior Authorization Information (2025)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"all services requiring prior authorization","quote":"A valid authorization number must be included on the claim form for all services requiring prior authorization.","document":"First Choice by Select Health of South Carolina — Claim Filing Manual"}]}'::jsonb, 'unknown', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-000a-4000-8000-00000000a00a'::uuid, 'Services requiring prior authorization (Note: Prior authorization requirements are applicable to secondary claims.)', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
