ialist care, the primary care physician must issue a referral before the patient''s visit to the specialist, other than for direct-access services or emergency care, and the referral must be for covered benefits under the plan. A palliative/home-visit physician seen as a specialist under such a plan needs the PCP referral on file before the home E/M visit. Referral requirement varies by plan (Aetna Open Access plans and some others do not require referrals). No codes are named. (4) Blanket rule: precertification is required whether Aetna is the primary or the secondary payer — the quoted bullet reads in full ''We require precertification when we''re the primary or secondary payer.'' (the quote below is the contiguous run available in the two-column source). Important for palliative practices where Aetna sits behind Medicare or another primary plan: a required precertification is not waived by Aetna''s secondary position. The same section repeats it for Innovation Health. No codes are named. (5) Blanket submission-timing rule. Where precertification is required for a service, Aetna requires the request to be submitted at least two weeks in advance; requests may be submitted through the Availity provider portal or by EMR-generated electronic request. Not a rule specific to any of the mapped codes — it governs any precertification a home-based palliative practice must obtain (for example, when a visit is delivered out of network under rule 1). The document does not name any of these codes. (6) Blanket rule on the life of an approval: where member eligibility and plan coverage for the requested procedure or service have not changed, a precertification approval is valid for six months in all states, unless Aetna says otherwise in the precertification decision. Relevant to home-based palliative practices tracking authorisation expiry across a long episode of care. Stated by situation, not by code. (7) Blanket rule: referrals should not be retroactive; the quoted sentence continues ''deny payment for retroactive referrals.'' A referral obtained after the home visit has already occurred may have its payment adjusted or denied. Applies in plans that require referrals; no codes are named.","appliesToService":"Coverage at an in-network benefit level for out-of-network provider or facility unless services are emergent","mappedFrom":"service-level rule mapped to this code","sourceDocument":"Aetna — Participating Provider Precertification List (updated August 1, 2026)","supportingQuotes":[{"label":"Referral policies -- additional referrals after an initial consultation","quote":"If the specialty visits will exceed the number of visits","document":"Aetna — Office Manual for Health Care Professionals (23.20.801.1 L, 12/19)"},{"label":"Referral policies -- referral for specialist care","quote":"direct-access services or emergency care, the primary care physician must issue a referral prior to the patient''s","document":"Aetna — Office Manual for Health Care Professionals (23.20.801.1 L, 12/19)"},{"label":"General information -- precertification when Aetna is primary or secondary payer","quote":"We require precertification when we''re the","document":"Aetna — Participating Provider Precertification List (updated August 1, 2026)"},{"label":"Submitting precertification requests","quote":"You must submit precertification requests at least two weeks in advance.","document":"Aetna — Participating Provider Precertification List (updated August 1, 2026)"},{"label":"Coverage changes and updates (precertification approvals)","quote":"If member eligibility and plan coverage for the procedure or service you asked for hasn''t changed, precertification approvals are valid for six months. This is true for all states.","document":"Aetna — Participating Provider Precertification List (updated August 1, 2026)"},{"label":"Referral policies -- retroactive referrals","quote":"Referrals should not be retroactive. We may adjust or","document":"Aetna — Office Manual for Health Care Professionals (23.20.801.1 L, 12/19)"}]}'::jsonb, 'varies', 0.75, DATE '2026-01-01', NULL, 'f1000000-000c-4000-8000-00000000a00c'::uuid, 'Coverage at an in-network benefit level for out-of-network provider or facility unless services are emergent', 'extract:round3-six-payers-2026-08'),
